From: slaren <slarengh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] soundwire: qcom: acknowledge interrupts before handling them

qcom_swrm_irq_handler() reads INTERRUPT_STATUS, handles every set bit and
only then writes the value it read at the start to INTERRUPT_CLEAR. An
event that re-asserts an already-set bit while it is being handled is
cleared without ever being seen.

This loses Peripheral re-attachment on x1e80100 (Surface Laptop 7, two
WSA884x on the WSA bus). When a clock-stop exit makes the amplifiers
lose sync, the handler sees CHANGE_ENUM_SLAVE_STATUS, marks them
UNATTACHED and starts enumerating (~3 ms). The hardware auto-enumerator
re-assigns device numbers 1 and 2 in that window. That re-latches
CHANGE_ENUM_SLAVE_STATUS, which the trailing clear then drops. Afterwards
SWRM_MCP_SLV_STATUS reads 0x14 with complete IDs while both Peripherals
stay UNATTACHED in software, and nothing re-syncs until reboot.

Clear NEW_SLAVE_ATTACHED/CHANGE_ENUM_SLAVE_STATUS before handling them, so
a status change that arrives during handling raises a new interrupt.
All other bits are still cleared after handling, unchanged.

Traced with kprobes on qcom_swrm_irq_handler/qcom_swrm_enumerate/
sdw_handle_slave_status and soundwire_qcom dynamic debug: three status
interrupts in 1.4 ms after resume, the third handled for 3.2 ms, no
further status interrupt, hardware ends attached.

Not yet tested. Draft for a local 7.3.1-1.6 build on top of
0004-soundwire-qcom-disable-irq-before-clk-gate.patch.
---
--- a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
@@ -51,6 +51,8 @@
 #define SWRM_INTERRUPT_STATUS_SLAVE_PEND_IRQ			BIT(0)
 #define SWRM_INTERRUPT_STATUS_NEW_SLAVE_ATTACHED		BIT(1)
 #define SWRM_INTERRUPT_STATUS_CHANGE_ENUM_SLAVE_STATUS		BIT(2)
+#define SWRM_INTERRUPT_ATTACH_EVENTS		(SWRM_INTERRUPT_STATUS_NEW_SLAVE_ATTACHED | \
+					 SWRM_INTERRUPT_STATUS_CHANGE_ENUM_SLAVE_STATUS)
 #define SWRM_INTERRUPT_STATUS_MASTER_CLASH_DET			BIT(3)
 #define SWRM_INTERRUPT_STATUS_RD_FIFO_OVERFLOW			BIT(4)
 #define SWRM_INTERRUPT_STATUS_RD_FIFO_UNDERFLOW			BIT(5)
@@ -726,6 +728,20 @@
 	intr_sts_masked = intr_sts & ctrl->intr_mask;
 
 	do {
+		/*
+		 * Acknowledge the attach-status events before handling them.
+		 * Handling CHANGE_ENUM_SLAVE_STATUS can take milliseconds
+		 * (enumeration, Peripheral status callbacks); if the
+		 * auto-enumerator re-attaches a Peripheral in that window, the
+		 * same bit re-latches, and clearing it afterwards with the stale
+		 * intr_sts drops the event: the Peripheral stays UNATTACHED in
+		 * software while SWRM_MCP_SLV_STATUS reports it attached.
+		 * Other events keep being cleared after handling (the
+		 * CMD_IGNORED path relies on its delay before the clear).
+		 */
+		ctrl->reg_write(ctrl, ctrl->reg_layout[SWRM_REG_INTERRUPT_CLEAR],
+				intr_sts & SWRM_INTERRUPT_ATTACH_EVENTS);
+
 		for (i = 0; i < SWRM_INTERRUPT_MAX; i++) {
 			value = intr_sts_masked & BIT(i);
 			if (!value)
@@ -846,7 +862,7 @@
 			}
 		}
 		ctrl->reg_write(ctrl, ctrl->reg_layout[SWRM_REG_INTERRUPT_CLEAR],
-				intr_sts);
+				intr_sts & ~SWRM_INTERRUPT_ATTACH_EVENTS);
 		ctrl->reg_read(ctrl, ctrl->reg_layout[SWRM_REG_INTERRUPT_STATUS],
 			       &intr_sts);
 		intr_sts_masked = intr_sts & ctrl->intr_mask;
